```mdl
verdict SyncSlackChannel: Syncs every bound channel, but with concurrency 2, a whole-operation failure on any binding, and no channel narrowing input.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-slack/src/types/SlackOperation.ts#SyncSlackChannel, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-slack/src/operations/sync.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-connector/src/Binding.ts#syncAll]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-slack/src/operations/sync.test.ts]
  walkthrough:
    - The operation takes `ConnectorSpec.SyncInput` (connection, priority) and returns `pulled.added`. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-slack/src/types/SlackOperation.ts#SyncSlackChannel
    - `Binding.syncAll` fans out over the connection's cursors with `SYNC_CONCURRENCY = 2`. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-connector/src/Binding.ts#syncAll
    - The handler fetches history since the cursor, maps it and appends it to the mirror feed. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-slack/src/operations/sync.ts
  note: |
    The input has `priority`, not `channel?: Ref<Channel>`. Concurrency is 2, not `TARGET_CONCURRENCY=3`.
    A failed binding records `lastError` on its cursor, but `syncAll` then fails the operation with that
    error. The error is `ConnectorSync.DatabaseMissingError`, not `IntegrationDatabaseMissingError`.
    Channels are materialized by `MaterializeSlackTarget` when a binding is created, not on first sync.
```

