```mdl
verdict F-3.1: The Channel is keyed by slack.com/conversationId and history starts empty, but it is created at materialization, not first sync.
  status: diverged
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-slack/src/operations/sync.ts#findOrCreateChannelForTarget, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-slack/src/operations/materialize-target.ts]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-slack/src/operations/sync.test.ts]
  note: |
    `findOrCreateChannelForTarget` creates the keyed Channel when the connector materializes a binding.
    Sync requires an existing target and returns `added: 0` when the target is not a Channel. The first
    sync passes `oldest: undefined`, so it fetches full history as the spec says.
```

